-14 10:40:36'),(4979,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which is an example of application software?',NULL,'A word processor is application software used to create and edit documents.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19911,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4980,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What does a computer file contain?',NULL,'A file is a named collection of stored digital information.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19915,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4981,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which unit is commonly used to measure computer storage?',NULL,'The byte is a standard unit used to measure digital data storage.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19919,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4982,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','How many bits make one byte?',NULL,'One byte consists of eight bits.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19923,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4983,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a bit?',NULL,'A bit is a binary digit that can represent 0 or 1.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19927,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4984,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which two digits are used in the binary number system?',NULL,'Binary numbers use only the digits 0 and 1.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19931,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4985,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is the binary representation of decimal 2?',NULL,'Decimal 2 is represented as 10 in binary.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19935,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4986,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is the binary representation of decimal 5?',NULL,'Decimal 5 equals 101 in binary.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19939,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4987,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which component performs arithmetic and logical operations?',NULL,'The Arithmetic Logic Unit performs arithmetic and logical operations within the CPU.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19943,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4988,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What does ALU stand for?',NULL,'ALU stands for Arithmetic Logic Unit.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19947,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4989,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which component temporarily holds instructions and data being processed?',NULL,'RAM temporarily stores data and instructions that the CPU is actively using.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19951,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4990,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which device is used to provide a computer with electrical power?',NULL,'The power supply converts and provides suitable electrical power to computer components.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19955,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4991,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a computer program?',NULL,'A program is a set of instructions that tells a computer what to do.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19959,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4992,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which key is commonly used to move to the next line while typing?',NULL,'The Enter key commonly starts a new line or confirms a command.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19963,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4993,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which key is commonly used to remove the character to the left of the cursor?',NULL,'Backspace removes the character immediately to the left of the cursor.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19967,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4994,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which key removes the character or item at the cursor position in many applications?',NULL,'The Delete key commonly removes selected items or characters at the cursor position.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19971,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4995,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which key is commonly used with other keys to create keyboard shortcuts?',NULL,'Ctrl is frequently combined with other keys to perform shortcuts.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19975,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4996,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What does the keyboard shortcut Ctrl+C usually do?',NULL,'Ctrl+C copies the selected content to the clipboard.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19979,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4997,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What does Ctrl+V usually do?',NULL,'Ctrl+V pastes content from the clipboard.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19983,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:36'),(4998,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What does Ctrl+X usually do?',NULL,'Ctrl+X cuts the selected content and places it on the clipboard.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19987,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:36','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(4999,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What does Ctrl+Z usually do?',NULL,'Ctrl+Z commonly reverses the most recent action.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19991,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5000,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which key is commonly used to refresh a web page?',NULL,'F5 is commonly used to refresh or reload a web page.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19995,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5001,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which function key commonly opens Help in many Windows applications?',NULL,'F1 is traditionally associated with opening Help in many applications.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,19999,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5002,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which device connects a computer to a network wirelessly?',NULL,'A Wi-Fi adapter enables a computer to communicate with wireless networks.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20003,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5003,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a network?',NULL,'A network connects computers or other devices so they can communicate and share resources.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20007,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5004,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is the Internet?',NULL,'The Internet is a worldwide system of interconnected computer networks.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20011,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5005,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which device directs data between different networks?',NULL,'A router forwards packets between different networks.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20015,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5006,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which device is commonly used to connect devices within a local network?',NULL,'A network switch connects devices on a local network and forwards data between them.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20019,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5007,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What does LAN stand for?',NULL,'LAN stands for Local Area Network.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20023,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5008,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What does WAN stand for?',NULL,'WAN stands for Wide Area Network.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20027,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5009,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which connection type uses a physical network cable?',NULL,'Ethernet commonly uses physical network cables to connect devices.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20031,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5010,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which technology is commonly used for short-range wireless connections between personal devices?',NULL,'Bluetooth is designed for short-range wireless communication between compatible devices.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20035,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5011,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a web browser?',NULL,'A web browser retrieves and displays web pages and other web content.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20039,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5012,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which of these is a web browser?',NULL,'Mozilla Firefox is a web browser used to access websites.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20043,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5013,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a search engine used for?',NULL,'A search engine helps users find information and web pages on the Internet.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20047,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5014,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What does URL stand for?',NULL,'URL stands for Uniform Resource Locator and identifies the location of a resource on the web.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20051,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5015,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is an email?',NULL,'Email is a system for sending and receiving electronic messages.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20055,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5016,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which symbol is required in a standard email address?',NULL,'The @ symbol separates the username from the domain in a standard email address.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20059,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5017,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a password used for?',NULL,'A password helps verify identity and protect access to accounts or systems.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20063,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5018,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which practice makes a password stronger?',NULL,'Long, unique passwords with varied characters are generally harder to guess.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20067,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5019,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a computer virus?',NULL,'A computer virus is malicious software capable of replicating and potentially spreading to other files or systems.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20071,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5020,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is antivirus software designed to do?',NULL,'Antivirus software helps detect, block, and remove malware.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20075,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5021,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is malware?',NULL,'Malware is a general term for software designed to harm, disrupt, or gain unauthorized access.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20079,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5022,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a firewall used for?',NULL,'A firewall filters network traffic according to security rules.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20083,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5023,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a backup?',NULL,'A backup is a separate copy of data used to restore information if the original is lost or damaged.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20087,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5024,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Why should important computer files be backed up?',NULL,'Backups provide a way to recover important data after accidental deletion, hardware failure, or other loss.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20091,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5025,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is cloud storage?',NULL,'Cloud storage keeps data on remote servers that can be accessed through a network such as the Internet.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20095,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5026,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which storage medium uses laser technology to read data?',NULL,'Optical discs such as CDs and DVDs use lasers to read stored data.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20099,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5027,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which device was commonly used to store small amounts of data using magnetic media?',NULL,'Floppy disks are removable magnetic storage media that were widely used for small data storage.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20103,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5028,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which component is often called the brain of the computer?',NULL,'The CPU is often called the brain of the computer because it executes instructions and controls processing.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20107,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5029,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a desktop computer?',NULL,'A desktop computer is generally designed for use at a stationary desk or workstation.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20111,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5030,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a laptop?',NULL,'A laptop is a portable personal computer with integrated components such as a display and keyboard.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20115,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5031,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which device allows a laptop to connect to an external display?',NULL,'An HDMI cable can carry digital video and audio to a compatible external display.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20119,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5032,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What does USB stand for?',NULL,'USB stands for Universal Serial Bus.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20123,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5033,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which port is commonly used to connect USB devices?',NULL,'A USB port is designed to connect compatible USB peripherals and devices.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20127,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5034,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a file extension?',NULL,'A file extension is the suffix of a filename that commonly indicates its file type or associated application.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20131,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5035,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which extension is commonly associated with a plain text file?',NULL,'The .txt extension is commonly used for plain text files.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20135,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5036,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which extension is commonly associated with an image file?',NULL,'The .jpg extension is commonly used for JPEG image files.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20139,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5037,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which extension is commonly associated with an audio file?',NULL,'The .mp3 extension is commonly used for compressed digital audio files.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20143,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5038,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which extension is commonly associated with a web page written in HTML?',NULL,'The .html extension is commonly used for HTML web pages.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20147,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5039,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a folder used for on a computer?',NULL,'Folders organize files and can contain other folders.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20151,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5040,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is the desktop in a graphical operating system?',NULL,'The desktop is the main graphical workspace where icons, windows, and other interface elements can appear.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20155,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5041,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is an icon in a graphical user interface?',NULL,'An icon visually represents an application, file, folder, device, or function.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20159,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5042,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a graphical user interface?',NULL,'A graphical user interface uses elements such as windows, icons, menus, and pointers for interaction.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20163,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5043,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a command-line interface?',NULL,'A command-line interface allows users to interact with a computer by entering text commands.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20167,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5044,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a software update?',NULL,'A software update can add features, fix bugs, or improve security and performance.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20171,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5045,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Why are operating system updates important?',NULL,'Operating system updates often include security patches, bug fixes, and other improvements.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20175,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5046,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a touchscreen?',NULL,'A touchscreen combines display output with touch-based input.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20179,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5047,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which device is used to record sound into a computer?',NULL,'A microphone captures sound and converts it into signals that a computer can process.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20183,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5048,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which device converts digital information into a paper document?',NULL,'A printer converts digital documents or images into physical output on paper.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20187,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5049,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which device converts a paper document into digital data?',NULL,'A scanner captures a physical document and converts its contents into digital form.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20191,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:37'),(5050,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a computer monitor\'s resolution?',NULL,'Display resolution describes the number of pixels used horizontally and vertically to form an image.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20195,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:37','2026-08-14 10:40:38'),(5051,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is screen brightness?',NULL,'Screen brightness controls how intensely the display emits light.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20199,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:38','2026-08-14 10:40:38'),(5052,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a pixel?',NULL,'A pixel is a picture element used to form digital images and displays.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20203,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:38','2026-08-14 10:40:38'),(5053,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a printer\'s DPI commonly used to describe?',NULL,'DPI, or dots per inch, is commonly used to describe printer resolution.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20207,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:38','2026-08-14 10:40:38'),(5054,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is CPU clock speed commonly measured in?',NULL,'CPU clock frequency is measured in hertz, commonly expressed as gigahertz.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20211,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:38','2026-08-14 10:40:38'),(5055,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What does GHz stand for?',NULL,'GHz stands for gigahertz, a unit of frequency equal to one billion hertz.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20215,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:38','2026-08-14 10:40:38'),(5056,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What does GB commonly stand for in computer storage?',NULL,'GB commonly means gigabyte, a unit used to express digital storage capacity.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20219,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:38','2026-08-14 10:40:38'),(5057,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which component is responsible for rendering graphics?',NULL,'A GPU, or Graphics Processing Unit, is specialized for processing and rendering graphics.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20223,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:38','2026-08-14 10:40:38'),(5058,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What does GPU stand for?',NULL,'GPU stands for Graphics Processing Unit.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20227,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:38','2026-08-14 10:40:38'),(5059,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which device can provide a computer with printed output and often scanning functions in one machine?',NULL,'A multifunction printer can combine printing, scanning, and sometimes copying or faxing functions.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20231,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:38','2026-08-14 10:40:38'),(5060,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','What is a USB flash drive mainly used for?',NULL,'A USB flash drive is a portable storage device used to save and transfer digital files.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20235,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:38','2026-08-14 10:40:38'),(5061,51,69,'mcq_single','medium','Which computer component helps keep the CPU cool?',NULL,'A heat sink absorbs and dissipates heat from the CPU, often with help from a fan.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20239,1,NULL,'2026-08-14 10:40:38','2026-08-14 10:40:38'),(5062,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which keyword declares a block-scoped variable that can be reassigned in JavaScript?',NULL,'The let keyword declares a block-scoped variable whose value can later be reassigned.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20244,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5063,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which keyword declares a block-scoped variable that cannot be reassigned?',NULL,'The const keyword creates a block-scoped binding that cannot be reassigned.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20249,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5064,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which operator checks both value and type equality in JavaScript?',NULL,'The strict equality operator === compares both the value and the type without coercion.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20253,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5065,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which method converts a JavaScript object into a JSON string?',NULL,'JSON.stringify() serializes a JavaScript value into a JSON-formatted string.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20256,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5066,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which method parses a JSON string into a JavaScript value?',NULL,'JSON.parse() converts valid JSON text into the corresponding JavaScript value.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20259,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5067,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which array method adds one or more elements to the end of an array?',NULL,'The push() method adds elements to the end of an array and returns its new length.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20265,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5068,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which array method removes the last element from an array?',NULL,'The pop() method removes and returns the last element of an array.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20267,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5069,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which array method removes the first element from an array?',NULL,'The shift() method removes and returns the first element of an array.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20272,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5070,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which array method adds elements to the beginning of an array?',NULL,'The unshift() method adds one or more elements to the beginning of an array.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20277,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5071,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','What does typeof null return in JavaScript?',NULL,'Due to a historical behavior in JavaScript, typeof null returns the string object.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20281,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5072,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','What is the result of typeof undefined?',NULL,'The typeof operator returns the string undefined for the primitive value undefined.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20284,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5073,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which value represents a number that is not a valid numeric result?',NULL,'NaN means Not-a-Number and represents an invalid or unrepresentable numeric result.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20288,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5074,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which global function checks whether a value is NaN without coercing its argument?',NULL,'Number.isNaN() returns true only when the supplied value is the numeric NaN value.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20292,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5075,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which operator returns the remainder after division?',NULL,'The remainder operator % returns the remainder left after division.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20296,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5076,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which operator performs exponentiation in modern JavaScript?',NULL,'The ** operator raises the left operand to the power of the right operand.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20300,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5077,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which value is a primitive BigInt literal?',NULL,'An integer literal followed by n, such as 100n, is a BigInt literal.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20303,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5078,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which statement exits the current loop immediately?',NULL,'The break statement terminates the nearest enclosing loop or switch statement.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20309,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5079,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which statement skips the remaining body of the current loop iteration?',NULL,'The continue statement skips to the next iteration of the nearest enclosing loop.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20312,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5080,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which keyword is used to define a function declaration?',NULL,'The function keyword introduces a JavaScript function declaration or expression.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20316,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5081,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which syntax creates an arrow function with one parameter and an expression body?',NULL,'The (x) => x * 2 syntax is an arrow function with an implicit return.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20320,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5082,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','What does an arrow function use for its lexical this value?',NULL,'Arrow functions do not bind their own this; they capture this from the surrounding lexical scope.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20325,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5083,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which method executes a callback for every element of an array without creating a transformed array?',NULL,'forEach() calls a callback once for each array element and does not return a transformed array.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20328,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5084,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which array method creates a new array containing elements that pass a test?',NULL,'filter() returns a new array containing elements for which the callback returns true.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20333,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5085,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which array method transforms each element into a new value?',NULL,'map() creates a new array by applying a callback to each element.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20335,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5086,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which array method reduces an array to a single accumulated value?',NULL,'reduce() applies a callback cumulatively to produce a single result.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20339,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5087,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which array method returns the first element that satisfies a condition?',NULL,'find() returns the first array element for which the callback returns true.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20344,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5088,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which array method returns true if at least one element satisfies a condition?',NULL,'some() returns true when at least one element makes the callback return true.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20348,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5089,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which array method returns true only if every element satisfies a condition?',NULL,'every() returns true only when the callback returns true for every array element.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20352,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5090,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which method checks whether an array contains a specific value using SameValueZero comparison?',NULL,'Array.prototype.includes() checks for a value using SameValueZero semantics.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20357,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5091,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which method returns the first index of a specified value in an array?',NULL,'indexOf() returns the first matching index or -1 if the value is not found.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20360,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5092,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which string method converts text to uppercase?',NULL,'toUpperCase() returns a new string with letters converted to uppercase.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20364,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5093,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which string method removes whitespace from both ends of a string?',NULL,'trim() removes whitespace from both the beginning and end of a string.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20367,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5094,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which string method checks whether a string starts with a specified substring?',NULL,'startsWith() returns true when a string begins with the specified substring.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20372,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5095,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which string method checks whether a string ends with a specified substring?',NULL,'endsWith() returns true when a string ends with the specified substring.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20375,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5096,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which string method returns the position of the first occurrence of a substring?',NULL,'String.prototype.indexOf() returns the first matching position or -1 when absent.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20381,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5097,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which method splits a string into an array using a separator?',NULL,'split() divides a string according to a separator and returns an array of substrings.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20383,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5098,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which operator is used for optional chaining?',NULL,'The ?. operator safely accesses a property or calls a method when the preceding value is not nullish.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20387,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5099,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which operator provides a fallback only when the left operand is null or undefined?',NULL,'The nullish coalescing operator ?? uses the right operand only when the left operand is null or undefined.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20393,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5100,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which syntax is used for a JavaScript template literal?',NULL,'Template literals are enclosed in backticks and support interpolation with ${...}.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20397,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5101,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','How do you embed an expression inside a template literal?',NULL,'Template literals use ${expression} for embedded expressions.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20400,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5102,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which object stores key-value pairs and has string or Symbol keys?',NULL,'A JavaScript object stores properties identified by string or Symbol keys.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20405,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5103,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which collection stores unique values?',NULL,'A Set collection stores unique values and ignores duplicate additions.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20408,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5104,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which collection stores key-value pairs and allows keys of any value type?',NULL,'Map stores key-value pairs and allows keys to be values of any JavaScript type.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20412,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5105,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which collection stores weakly held object keys mapped to values?',NULL,'WeakMap associates values with object keys using weak references to those keys.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20416,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5106,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which collection stores weakly held objects as unique values?',NULL,'WeakSet stores objects as unique values using weak references.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20421,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5107,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which syntax destructures properties from an object?',NULL,'Object destructuring uses braces to extract properties from an object into variables.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20423,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5108,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which syntax destructures elements from an array?',NULL,'Array destructuring uses brackets to assign array elements to variables.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20428,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5109,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which syntax spreads array elements into another array?',NULL,'The spread syntax ... expands iterable elements into a new array literal.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20431,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5110,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which syntax collects remaining function arguments into an array?',NULL,'A rest parameter written as ...args collects remaining arguments into an array.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20436,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5111,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','What does Array.isArray([]) return?',NULL,'Array.isArray([]) returns true because the supplied value is an Array.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20441,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5112,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which keyword handles exceptions thrown inside a try block?',NULL,'The catch clause handles exceptions thrown during execution of the associated try block.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20443,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5113,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which block executes whether or not an exception occurs?',NULL,'A finally block runs after try/catch processing regardless of whether an exception occurred.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20448,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5114,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which statement explicitly throws an exception?',NULL,'The throw statement interrupts normal execution by throwing a specified value as an exception.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20451,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5115,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which built-in constructor creates a standard Error object?',NULL,'The Error constructor creates an Error object containing information about an error.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20455,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5116,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which keyword waits for a Promise to settle inside an async function?',NULL,'The await keyword pauses the async function until the awaited Promise settles.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20460,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5117,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','What does an async function always return?',NULL,'An async function always returns a Promise, even when it returns a non-Promise value.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20464,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5118,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which Promise state means the operation has completed successfully?',NULL,'A Promise is fulfilled when its operation completes successfully with a value.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20468,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5119,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which Promise state means the operation has completed unsuccessfully?',NULL,'A Promise is rejected when its operation fails with a reason.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20473,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5120,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which Promise state represents an operation that has not yet completed?',NULL,'A newly created Promise is pending until it becomes fulfilled or rejected.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20475,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5121,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which method handles successful fulfillment of a Promise?',NULL,'Promise.prototype.then() registers handlers for fulfillment and can also handle chaining.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20480,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5122,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which method handles Promise rejection?',NULL,'Promise.prototype.catch() registers a rejection handler for a Promise chain.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20484,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5123,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which Promise method runs a callback after settlement regardless of outcome?',NULL,'Promise.prototype.finally() runs after a Promise is settled whether it is fulfilled or rejected.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20488,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5124,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which Promise method waits for all input promises to fulfill and rejects if one rejects?',NULL,'Promise.all() fulfills when every input fulfills and rejects when any input rejects.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20492,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5125,95,109,'mcq_single','hard','Which Promise method fulfills when the first input Promise fulfills and rejects only if all reject?',NULL,'Promise.any() fulfills when the first input fulfills and rejects with an AggregateError if all reject.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20497,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5126,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which Promise method settles when the first input Promise settles?',NULL,'Promise.race() settles as soon as the first input Promise settles.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20499,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5127,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which Promise method returns results for all inputs regardless of fulfillment or rejection?',NULL,'Promise.allSettled() fulfills after all input promises settle and reports each outcome.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20503,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5128,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which function schedules a callback after at least the specified delay using the timer mechanism?',NULL,'setTimeout() schedules a callback to run after the specified minimum delay.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20507,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5129,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which function repeatedly schedules a callback at approximately regular intervals?',NULL,'setInterval() repeatedly schedules a callback at approximately the specified interval.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20512,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5130,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which function cancels a timeout created by setTimeout()?',NULL,'clearTimeout() cancels a pending timeout created by setTimeout().',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20515,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5131,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which function cancels an interval created by setInterval()?',NULL,'clearInterval() cancels a repeating interval created by setInterval().',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20519,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5132,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which keyword creates a class declaration?',NULL,'The class keyword defines a JavaScript class.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20524,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5133,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which method is automatically called when a class instance is created with new?',NULL,'The constructor() method runs when a class is instantiated with new.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20528,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5134,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which keyword refers to the parent class in a derived class?',NULL,'The super keyword accesses the parent class constructor and methods.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20533,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5135,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which keyword establishes class inheritance?',NULL,'The extends keyword creates a subclass from another class.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20536,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5136,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which operator checks whether an object is an instance of a constructor or class?',NULL,'The instanceof operator tests the prototype chain relationship between an object and a constructor\'s prototype.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20540,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5137,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which built-in object represents a date and time value?',NULL,'The built-in Date object represents a specific point in time and provides date and time operations.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20544,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5138,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which method gets the four-digit year in local time from a Date object?',NULL,'getFullYear() returns the full numeric year in local time.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20548,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5139,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which Date method returns the month index in local time?',NULL,'getMonth() returns a zero-based month index from 0 for January through 11 for December.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20551,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5140,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which Math method rounds a number downward toward negative infinity?',NULL,'Math.floor() returns the greatest integer less than or equal to its argument.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20555,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5141,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which Math method rounds a number upward toward positive infinity?',NULL,'Math.ceil() returns the smallest integer greater than or equal to its argument.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20560,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5142,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which Math method removes the fractional part by truncating toward zero?',NULL,'Math.trunc() removes the fractional digits and moves toward zero.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20566,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5143,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which global function converts a numeric string to an integer using a specified radix?',NULL,'parseInt() parses a string and returns an integer, with an optional radix specifying the numeral system.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20567,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5144,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which function converts a numeric string to a floating-point number?',NULL,'parseFloat() parses a string and returns a floating-point number when possible.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20572,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5145,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which object represents a regular expression pattern in JavaScript?',NULL,'RegExp is the built-in JavaScript object used to represent regular expression patterns.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20576,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5146,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which regex flag enables case-insensitive matching?',NULL,'The i flag makes regular expression matching case-insensitive.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20580,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5147,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which regex flag enables global matching rather than stopping after the first match?',NULL,'The g flag makes a regular expression search globally for matches.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20583,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5148,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which method tests whether a regular expression matches a string?',NULL,'RegExp.prototype.test() returns true when the regular expression finds a match in the string.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20588,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5149,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which JavaScript feature lets a function remember variables from its outer lexical scope?',NULL,'A closure allows a function to retain access to variables from its surrounding lexical environment.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20592,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5150,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','What is hoisting in JavaScript?',NULL,'Hoisting describes how declarations are processed before execution, affecting when certain bindings can be accessed.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20596,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5151,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','What does the event loop primarily coordinate in JavaScript?',NULL,'The event loop coordinates execution of queued asynchronous work with the JavaScript call stack.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20600,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5152,95,109,'mcq_single','hard','Which queue is associated with Promise reaction callbacks?',NULL,'Promise reactions are scheduled as microtasks, which are processed after the current synchronous job before many task-queue callbacks.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20603,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5153,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which method creates a new object with a specified prototype object?',NULL,'Object.create() creates a new object whose internal prototype is the supplied object.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20607,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5154,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which method returns an array of an object\'s own enumerable string-keyed property names?',NULL,'Object.keys() returns the own enumerable string-keyed property names of an object.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20611,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5155,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which method returns an array containing an object\'s own enumerable string-keyed key-value pairs?',NULL,'Object.entries() returns arrays containing each own enumerable string-keyed property and its value.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20615,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5156,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which method returns an array of an object\'s own enumerable string-keyed property values?',NULL,'Object.values() returns the values of an object\'s own enumerable string-keyed properties.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20619,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5157,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which statement creates a JavaScript module export using a named export?',NULL,'The export statement with braces creates a named module export.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20623,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5158,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which statement imports a named export called value from a module?',NULL,'The import { value } syntax imports a named export called value from the specified module.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20628,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5159,95,109,'mcq_single','easy','Which browser API selects the first DOM element matching a CSS selector?',NULL,'document.querySelector() returns the first element matching the supplied CSS selector.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20632,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5160,95,109,'mcq_single','medium','Which browser API selects all DOM elements matching a CSS selector and returns a NodeList?',NULL,'document.querySelectorAll() returns a static NodeList containing elements that match the selector.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20635,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:51:56','2026-08-15 18:51:56'),(5161,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which keyword is used to define a function in Python?',NULL,'The def keyword starts a Python function definition.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20640,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5162,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which keyword is used to create a class in Python?',NULL,'The class keyword is used to define a Python class.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20644,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5163,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which symbol starts a single-line comment in Python?',NULL,'Python uses the hash character # to begin a single-line comment.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20648,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5164,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which function returns the number of items in a Python collection?',NULL,'The built-in len() function returns the number of items in a collection or characters in a string.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20653,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5165,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which built-in function displays output in Python?',NULL,'The print() function writes the supplied values to standard output.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20658,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5166,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which built-in function reads a line of text from standard input?',NULL,'The input() function reads a line from standard input and returns it as a string.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20660,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5167,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which Python type stores an ordered, mutable collection of items?',NULL,'A list is an ordered and mutable collection in Python.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20664,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5168,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which Python type stores an ordered, immutable collection of items?',NULL,'A tuple is an ordered collection whose elements cannot be changed after creation.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20669,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5169,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which Python collection stores unique elements without using key-value pairs?',NULL,'A set stores unique hashable elements and does not use key-value pairs.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20673,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5170,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which Python type stores key-value pairs?',NULL,'A dictionary stores data as key-value pairs.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20675,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5171,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which value represents the absence of a value in Python?',NULL,'None is Python\'s singleton value commonly used to represent the absence of a value.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20681,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5172,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','What is the result of type(10) in Python?',NULL,'The literal 10 is an integer, so type(10) is int.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20685,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5173,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which operator performs exponentiation in Python?',NULL,'The ** operator raises the left operand to the power of the right operand.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20688,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5174,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which operator performs floor division in Python?',NULL,'The // operator performs floor division, returning the floor of the quotient.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20693,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5175,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which operator returns the remainder of a division in Python?',NULL,'The % operator returns the remainder after division.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20697,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5176,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which operator checks equality between two Python values?',NULL,'The == operator compares two values for equality.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20700,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5177,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which operator checks object identity in Python?',NULL,'The is operator checks whether two references point to the same object.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20704,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5178,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which keyword creates a conditional branch in Python?',NULL,'The if keyword begins a conditional statement.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20707,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5179,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which keyword provides an alternative branch when an if condition is false?',NULL,'The else clause executes when the preceding if and elif conditions are false.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20711,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5180,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which keyword tests another condition after an if in Python?',NULL,'Python uses elif to test another condition when earlier conditions are false.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20716,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5181,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which loop iterates directly over items in an iterable?',NULL,'The for statement iterates over items produced by an iterable.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20720,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5182,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which Python loop continues while a condition is true?',NULL,'The while statement repeatedly executes its body while its condition remains true.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20725,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5183,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which statement exits the nearest loop immediately?',NULL,'The break statement terminates the nearest enclosing loop.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20728,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5184,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which statement skips to the next iteration of a loop?',NULL,'The continue statement skips the rest of the current iteration and proceeds to the next one.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20732,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5185,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which statement does nothing and serves as a placeholder?',NULL,'The pass statement performs no operation and is commonly used as a placeholder.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20736,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5186,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which function generates a sequence of integers commonly used in loops?',NULL,'range() produces an immutable sequence-like range of integers.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20740,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5187,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','What type does range(5) return in Python 3?',NULL,'In Python 3, range(5) creates a range object rather than a list.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20745,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5188,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which syntax creates a list containing the squares of numbers from 0 through 4?',NULL,'The list comprehension [x*x for x in range(5)] calculates a square for each value from 0 through 4.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20748,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5189,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which syntax creates a dictionary comprehension mapping each number to its square?',NULL,'Dictionary comprehensions use the form {key: value for item in iterable}.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20751,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5190,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which method adds one item to the end of a Python list?',NULL,'list.append() adds one item to the end of a list.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20756,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5191,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which list method inserts an item at a specified position?',NULL,'list.insert(index, value) inserts a value before the specified index.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20759,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5192,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which list method removes and returns the last item by default?',NULL,'list.pop() removes and returns the last element when no index is supplied.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20765,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5193,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which list method removes the first matching value?',NULL,'list.remove(value) removes the first occurrence of the specified value.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20768,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5194,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which list method sorts the list in place?',NULL,'list.sort() sorts the existing list in place.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20771,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5195,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which built-in function returns a new sorted list without modifying the original iterable?',NULL,'sorted() returns a new sorted list and leaves the original iterable unchanged.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20776,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5196,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which string method converts all letters to lowercase?',NULL,'str.lower() returns a lowercase version of the string.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20779,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5197,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which string method removes whitespace from both ends?',NULL,'str.strip() removes leading and trailing whitespace by default.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20783,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5198,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which string method splits text into a list using a separator?',NULL,'str.split() divides a string into a list of substrings using the specified separator.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20788,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5199,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which string method joins an iterable of strings using the calling string as the separator?',NULL,'str.join(iterable) concatenates strings with the calling string placed between them.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20792,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5200,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which syntax creates a raw string literal in Python?',NULL,'An r prefix creates a raw string literal in which most backslashes are treated literally.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20795,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5201,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which string formatting syntax uses an f prefix?',NULL,'An f-string begins with f or F and allows expressions inside braces.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20799,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5202,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which Python function converts a string such as \'42\' to an integer?',NULL,'The int() constructor converts a compatible value such as \'42\' into an integer.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20805,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5203,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which Python function converts a compatible numeric value to a floating-point number?',NULL,'The float() constructor creates a floating-point number from a compatible value.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20807,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5204,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which built-in function converts a value to a string?',NULL,'The str() constructor returns a string representation of a value.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20812,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5205,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which built-in function returns the largest item from an iterable?',NULL,'The max() function returns the largest item according to normal ordering or a supplied key.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20817,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5206,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which built-in function returns the smallest item from an iterable?',NULL,'The min() function returns the smallest item according to normal ordering or a supplied key.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20819,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5207,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which built-in function calculates the sum of numeric items?',NULL,'The sum() function adds items from an iterable, starting from zero by default.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20824,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5208,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which built-in function returns an iterator of pairs containing indexes and values?',NULL,'enumerate() yields pairs containing a count and the corresponding item.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20828,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5209,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which built-in function combines multiple iterables element by element?',NULL,'zip() creates an iterator that aggregates elements from multiple iterables by position.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20832,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5210,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which built-in function returns a Boolean result from a truth test on any item?',NULL,'any() returns True if at least one element of the iterable is truthy.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20835,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5211,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which built-in function returns True only when all items in an iterable are truthy?',NULL,'all() returns True when every element of the iterable is truthy or the iterable is empty.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20839,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5212,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which keyword defines an anonymous function in Python?',NULL,'The lambda keyword creates a small anonymous function expression.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20843,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5213,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','What does a lambda expression return when called?',NULL,'A lambda function evaluates its single expression and returns that expression\'s value.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20848,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5214,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which keyword is used to import a module?',NULL,'The import statement loads a module so its contents can be accessed.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20853,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5215,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which statement imports a module under an alias?',NULL,'Python supports aliases with the syntax import module as alias.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20855,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5216,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which statement imports a specific name from a module?',NULL,'The from module import name syntax imports a particular name from a module.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20859,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5217,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which special variable contains the current module\'s name?',NULL,'Python sets __name__ to the module\'s name; it becomes \'__main__\' when the file is run as the main program.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20864,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5218,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','What is the purpose of if __name__ == \'__main__\': in a Python file?',NULL,'The condition is true when the file is executed as the main program rather than imported as a module.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20868,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5219,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which keyword begins an exception-handling block?',NULL,'The try statement begins a block whose exceptions can be handled by except clauses.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20871,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5220,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which keyword handles a matching exception after try?',NULL,'Python uses except clauses to catch and handle exceptions raised in a try block.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20876,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5221,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which block runs whether an exception occurs or not?',NULL,'The finally block executes after the try statement completes, whether an exception occurred or not.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20880,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5222,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which keyword explicitly raises an exception?',NULL,'The raise statement explicitly raises an exception in Python.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20883,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5223,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which built-in exception is raised when an integer division or modulo operation uses zero as the divisor?',NULL,'Python raises ZeroDivisionError for division or modulo by zero.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20888,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5224,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which exception is raised when a sequence index is outside its valid range?',NULL,'IndexError occurs when a sequence index is out of range.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20892,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5225,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which exception is commonly raised when a dictionary key is not found?',NULL,'KeyError is raised when a dictionary lookup does not find the requested key.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20897,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5226,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which exception occurs when an operation receives an argument of an inappropriate type?',NULL,'TypeError indicates that an operation or function received a value of an inappropriate type.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20899,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5227,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which exception occurs when a value has the correct type but an inappropriate value?',NULL,'ValueError is used when the type is appropriate but the value itself is invalid for the operation.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20904,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5228,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which keyword is used to create a generator function that yields values lazily?',NULL,'The yield keyword produces a value from a generator function and suspends its execution until the next request.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20907,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5229,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','What does calling a generator function normally return before iteration?',NULL,'Calling a generator function returns a generator object; its body executes as iteration requests values.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20912,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5230,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which built-in function retrieves the next item from an iterator?',NULL,'The next() function requests the next item from an iterator.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20915,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5231,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which built-in function creates an iterator from an iterable?',NULL,'The iter() function returns an iterator for an iterable object.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20919,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5232,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which protocol method returns an iterator for an object?',NULL,'An iterable object commonly implements __iter__() to return an iterator.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20924,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5233,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which protocol method returns the next item from an iterator?',NULL,'An iterator implements __next__() to return the next item or raise StopIteration.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20927,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5234,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which exception signals that an iterator has no more items?',NULL,'StopIteration signals that an iterator has been exhausted.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20932,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5235,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which decorator converts a method into a property accessed like an attribute?',NULL,'The @property decorator creates a managed attribute accessed without calling the method explicitly.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20936,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5236,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which decorator is used to define a static method inside a class?',NULL,'The @staticmethod decorator creates a method that does not receive an implicit instance or class argument.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20940,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5237,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which decorator defines a class method that receives the class as its first argument?',NULL,'The @classmethod decorator creates a method whose first argument conventionally receives the class object.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20943,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5238,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which first parameter convention is commonly used for an instance method?',NULL,'self is the conventional name for the first parameter of an instance method and refers to the instance.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20947,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5239,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which first parameter convention is commonly used for a class method?',NULL,'cls is the conventional name for the first parameter of a class method and refers to the class.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20952,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5240,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which special method initializes a newly created instance after object creation?',NULL,'__init__() initializes an instance after it has been created.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20956,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5241,95,111,'mcq_single','hard','Which special method controls creation of a new instance before __init__()?',NULL,'__new__() is responsible for creating a new instance and runs before __init__().',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20959,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5242,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which keyword is used in a subclass declaration to inherit from a base class?',NULL,'Python specifies inheritance by placing base classes in parentheses after the subclass name.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20965,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5243,95,111,'mcq_single','hard','Which function returns the method resolution order of a class?',NULL,'The mro() method returns the method resolution order used for attribute and method lookup.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20967,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5244,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which built-in function checks whether an object is an instance of a specified class or tuple of classes?',NULL,'isinstance() checks whether an object is an instance of a class or one of the classes in a tuple.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20972,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5245,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which built-in function checks whether a class is a subclass of another class?',NULL,'issubclass() returns True when the first class is derived from the second class or one of its subclasses.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20975,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5246,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which data structure provides insertion-ordered key-value mappings in modern Python dictionaries?',NULL,'Python dictionaries preserve insertion order as part of the language specification in modern Python versions.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20979,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5247,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which dictionary method safely returns a value for a key and can accept a default?',NULL,'dict.get(key, default) returns the value for a key or the supplied default when the key is absent.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20984,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5248,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which dictionary method returns and removes a key-value pair, with the last pair used by default?',NULL,'dict.popitem() removes and returns a key-value pair, using the last inserted pair by default.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20989,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5249,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which set method removes an element without raising an error if it is absent?',NULL,'set.discard() removes an element if present and does nothing when it is absent.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20992,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5250,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which set method removes an element and raises KeyError if it is absent?',NULL,'set.remove() raises KeyError when the specified element is not present.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20996,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5251,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which operator performs set union in Python?',NULL,'The | operator computes the union of two sets.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,20999,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5252,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which operator performs set intersection in Python?',NULL,'The & operator computes the intersection of two sets.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21004,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5253,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which operator performs set difference in Python?',NULL,'The - operator returns elements present in the left set but not the right set.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21007,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5254,95,111,'mcq_single','medium','Which operator performs symmetric difference between two sets?',NULL,'The ^ operator returns elements that are in either set but not in both.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21013,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5255,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which module provides regular expression operations in Python\'s standard library?',NULL,'The re module provides regular expression matching and substitution operations.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21016,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5256,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which module provides common mathematical functions such as sqrt() and sin()?',NULL,'The math module provides many standard mathematical functions and constants for real numbers.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21019,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5257,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which module provides pseudo-random number generation functions?',NULL,'The random module provides functions for generating pseudo-random values.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21023,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5258,95,111,'mcq_single','easy','Which module provides statistical functions such as mean() and median()?',NULL,'The statistics module provides functions for common statistical calculations.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21028,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 18:54:15','2026-08-15 18:54:15'),(5259,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is the primary purpose of a database?',NULL,'A database is designed to store, organize, retrieve, and manage data efficiently.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21031,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5260,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which language is primarily used to query relational databases?',NULL,'SQL, or Structured Query Language, is the standard language used to work with relational databases.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21036,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5261,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL command retrieves data from a table?',NULL,'SELECT is used to retrieve rows and columns from one or more database tables.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21040,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5262,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL command adds new rows to a table?',NULL,'INSERT adds new records to a database table.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21044,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5263,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL command modifies existing rows?',NULL,'UPDATE changes values in existing rows that match its condition.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21048,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29');
INSERT INTO `bank_questions` VALUES (5264,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL command removes rows from a table?',NULL,'DELETE removes rows from a table, optionally based on a WHERE condition.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21052,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5265,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL command creates a new table?',NULL,'CREATE TABLE defines a new table and its columns and constraints.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21056,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5266,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL command removes an entire table and its definition?',NULL,'DROP TABLE removes the table definition and its stored data.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21061,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5267,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL clause filters rows based on a condition?',NULL,'The WHERE clause restricts rows according to a specified condition.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21064,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5268,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL clause sorts query results?',NULL,'ORDER BY sorts the result set using one or more specified columns.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21068,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5269,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL clause groups rows that share values?',NULL,'GROUP BY groups rows with matching values so aggregate calculations can be performed per group.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21071,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5270,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','Which SQL clause filters groups after aggregation?',NULL,'HAVING filters grouped results after GROUP BY and aggregate calculations.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21076,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5271,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL keyword removes duplicate rows from a result set?',NULL,'DISTINCT eliminates duplicate rows from the selected result set.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21080,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5272,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL aggregate function counts rows or non-null values?',NULL,'COUNT() returns the number of rows or non-null values depending on its argument.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21084,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5273,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL aggregate function calculates the arithmetic mean?',NULL,'AVG() calculates the average of numeric values in a group.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21087,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5274,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL aggregate function returns the largest value?',NULL,'MAX() returns the greatest value among the selected values.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21092,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5275,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL aggregate function returns the smallest value?',NULL,'MIN() returns the smallest value among the selected values.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21095,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5276,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL aggregate function calculates a total?',NULL,'SUM() calculates the total of numeric values.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21100,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5277,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is a primary key used for?',NULL,'A primary key uniquely identifies each row in a table.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21103,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5278,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which constraint prevents duplicate values in a column?',NULL,'The UNIQUE constraint prevents duplicate values in the constrained column or column combination.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21107,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5279,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which constraint ensures a column cannot contain NULL?',NULL,'NOT NULL requires every row to contain a non-null value in that column.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21111,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5280,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which constraint defines a value automatically when no value is supplied?',NULL,'A DEFAULT constraint supplies a specified value when an insert does not provide one.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21116,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5281,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','Which constraint enforces a Boolean condition on column values?',NULL,'A CHECK constraint requires inserted or updated values to satisfy a specified condition.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21120,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5282,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is a foreign key primarily used to represent?',NULL,'A foreign key links a column to a key in another table, enforcing referential relationships.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21123,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5283,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is a candidate key?',NULL,'A candidate key is a minimal set of attributes that uniquely identifies each row and can therefore serve as a primary key.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21127,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5284,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is a composite key?',NULL,'A composite key consists of two or more columns used together to uniquely identify a row.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21131,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5285,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What does NULL generally represent in a relational database?',NULL,'NULL represents the absence of a known value and is distinct from zero or an empty string.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21137,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5286,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','Which comparison should be used to test for NULL in standard SQL?',NULL,'SQL uses IS NULL to test whether a value is NULL.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21140,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5287,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is a database schema?',NULL,'A schema describes the logical organization of database objects such as tables, views, and constraints.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21143,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5288,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is normalization intended to reduce?',NULL,'Normalization organizes relational data to reduce unnecessary redundancy and modification anomalies.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21147,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5289,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','Which normal form requires atomic values and no repeating groups in a relation?',NULL,'First Normal Form requires each field to contain atomic values and removes repeating groups.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21151,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5290,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','Which normal form removes partial dependency on part of a composite key?',NULL,'Second Normal Form requires 1NF and removes partial dependencies on a portion of a composite candidate key.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21156,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5291,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','Which normal form removes transitive dependencies of non-key attributes on a key?',NULL,'Third Normal Form removes transitive dependencies of non-key attributes on candidate keys.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21161,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5292,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is denormalization?',NULL,'Denormalization intentionally adds some redundancy to improve performance or simplify certain queries.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21163,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5293,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is an index primarily used for?',NULL,'Indexes provide data structures that can speed up searches, filtering, joins, and ordering.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21167,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5294,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is a common trade-off of adding indexes?',NULL,'Indexes consume storage and generally require maintenance when indexed data is inserted, updated, or deleted.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21171,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5295,95,112,'mcq_single','hard','What is a clustered index conceptually associated with?',NULL,'A clustered index determines how table rows are organized according to the index key in systems that support clustered storage.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21175,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5296,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is a database view?',NULL,'A view is a stored query definition that presents data as a virtual table.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21179,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5297,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL statement creates a view?',NULL,'CREATE VIEW defines a view based on a query.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21183,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5298,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is a stored procedure?',NULL,'A stored procedure is a named database-side program containing SQL and possibly procedural logic.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21187,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5299,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is a database trigger?',NULL,'A trigger automatically executes associated logic when specified database events occur.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21191,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5300,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is a transaction?',NULL,'A transaction groups related database operations into a logical unit that can be committed or rolled back.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21195,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5301,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What does COMMIT do in a transaction?',NULL,'COMMIT successfully ends a transaction and makes its changes durable according to the database system\'s guarantees.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21199,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5302,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What does ROLLBACK do?',NULL,'ROLLBACK reverses changes made by the current transaction that have not been committed.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21203,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5303,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What does ACID stand for in database transactions?',NULL,'ACID describes four key transaction properties: Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, and Durability.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21207,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5304,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which ACID property means a transaction is all-or-nothing?',NULL,'Atomicity ensures that a transaction\'s operations are completed as a unit or none are applied.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21212,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5305,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which ACID property ensures committed changes survive failures?',NULL,'Durability means committed transaction changes are preserved even after a failure, subject to the DBMS guarantees.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21218,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5306,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','Which ACID property separates concurrent transactions from interfering with one another?',NULL,'Isolation controls how concurrent transactions interact and what intermediate states they can observe.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21219,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5307,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','Which ACID property requires transactions to preserve database rules and constraints?',NULL,'Consistency requires a transaction to move the database from one valid state to another valid state according to its constraints.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21223,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5308,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is a deadlock in a database?',NULL,'A deadlock occurs when transactions form a cycle of waiting for resources held by one another.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21227,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5309,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is concurrency control used for?',NULL,'Concurrency control coordinates simultaneous transactions to maintain correctness and isolation.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21231,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5310,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is a transaction isolation level?',NULL,'An isolation level specifies what effects one concurrent transaction may observe from another.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21235,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5311,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','Which anomaly occurs when a transaction reads data that another transaction has changed but not committed?',NULL,'A dirty read occurs when a transaction reads uncommitted changes made by another transaction.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21239,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5312,95,112,'mcq_single','hard','Which anomaly occurs when the same row is read twice and gives different committed values within one transaction?',NULL,'A non-repeatable read occurs when a row read earlier is changed and committed by another transaction before it is read again.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21244,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5313,95,112,'mcq_single','hard','Which anomaly involves newly appearing or disappearing rows that match a repeated query condition?',NULL,'A phantom read occurs when repeated range queries return a different set of rows because another transaction inserted or removed matching rows.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21248,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5314,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is a join in SQL used for?',NULL,'A join combines rows from tables based on a related condition.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21251,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5315,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which join returns only rows with matching values on both sides?',NULL,'INNER JOIN returns rows where the join condition matches in both joined tables.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21255,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5316,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which join returns all rows from the left table and matching rows from the right table?',NULL,'LEFT JOIN preserves all rows from the left table and adds matching right-side values when available.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21260,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5317,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which join returns all rows from the right table and matching rows from the left table?',NULL,'RIGHT JOIN preserves all rows from the right table and includes matching rows from the left table.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21263,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5318,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','Which join produces the Cartesian product of two tables?',NULL,'CROSS JOIN combines every row from the first table with every row from the second table.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21268,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5319,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is a self join?',NULL,'A self join uses the same table more than once in a query, typically with aliases.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21271,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5320,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What does a subquery represent?',NULL,'A subquery is a query embedded inside another SQL statement.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21275,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5321,95,112,'mcq_single','hard','What is a correlated subquery?',NULL,'A correlated subquery depends on values from the outer query and may be evaluated in relation to each outer row.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21279,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5322,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is a primary purpose of the SQL GROUP BY clause?',NULL,'GROUP BY forms groups of rows with equal grouping values for aggregate calculations.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21283,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5323,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','Which SQL clause is evaluated conceptually before GROUP BY to filter individual rows?',NULL,'WHERE filters individual rows before grouping and aggregation in the logical query processing order.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21287,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5324,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is a database constraint?',NULL,'Constraints enforce rules that help maintain data integrity.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21291,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5325,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is referential integrity?',NULL,'Referential integrity ensures that foreign-key values correctly reference existing related rows or satisfy the allowed null rules.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21295,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5326,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is a surrogate key?',NULL,'A surrogate key is an artificial identifier created for database records rather than derived from business meaning.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21299,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:29','2026-08-15 19:08:29'),(5327,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is a natural key?',NULL,'A natural key uses meaningful real-world data, such as a unique code, to identify a record.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21303,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5328,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is cardinality in a relational relationship?',NULL,'Cardinality describes how many instances of one entity can be associated with instances of another entity.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21307,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5329,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which relationship allows one row in one table to relate to many rows in another?',NULL,'A one-to-many relationship allows one parent row to be associated with multiple child rows.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21312,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5330,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','Which table is commonly used to implement a many-to-many relationship?',NULL,'A junction table stores associations between rows of the two participating tables.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21315,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5331,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is a data type in a database column?',NULL,'A column\'s data type specifies what kind of values can be stored and how they are represented.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21319,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5332,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL data type is commonly used for whole numbers?',NULL,'INTEGER is a standard SQL numeric type used for whole-number values.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21323,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5333,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL type is commonly used for variable-length character data?',NULL,'VARCHAR stores variable-length character strings up to a specified maximum length in many SQL systems.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21327,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5334,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL type is designed to store calendar dates?',NULL,'DATE represents calendar date values without a time-of-day component.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21331,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5335,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL type commonly represents time of day without a date?',NULL,'TIME represents a time-of-day value in SQL systems that support the standard type.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21335,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5336,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','Which SQL type represents both date and time in many relational systems?',NULL,'DATETIME is commonly used by database systems to store both date and time components.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21339,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5337,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is a database backup?',NULL,'A backup is a recoverable copy of database information used to restore data after loss or corruption.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21343,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5338,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is database recovery?',NULL,'Database recovery uses logs, backups, and other mechanisms to restore a consistent state after failures.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21347,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5339,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is a transaction log used for?',NULL,'A transaction log records changes and transaction information that can support recovery and durability.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21351,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5340,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is database replication?',NULL,'Replication maintains synchronized or asynchronously updated copies of database data on multiple systems.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21355,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5341,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is horizontal scaling of a database?',NULL,'Horizontal scaling adds or distributes work across multiple machines or nodes.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21359,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5342,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is vertical scaling of a database?',NULL,'Vertical scaling increases resources such as CPU, memory, or storage on a single system.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21363,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5343,95,112,'mcq_single','hard','What is database sharding?',NULL,'Sharding partitions data across multiple nodes so different nodes handle different subsets of the data.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21367,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5344,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is a database partition?',NULL,'Partitioning divides large database objects into smaller pieces that can improve management and sometimes performance.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21371,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5345,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is a query optimizer?',NULL,'A query optimizer evaluates possible execution plans and chooses one it estimates will be efficient.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21375,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5346,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is an execution plan?',NULL,'An execution plan describes operations such as scans, joins, and sorts used to execute a query.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21379,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5347,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is a full table scan?',NULL,'A full table scan examines rows throughout the table rather than locating matching rows through a suitable index.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21383,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5348,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is SQL injection?',NULL,'SQL injection occurs when untrusted input is incorporated into SQL in a way that allows unintended SQL manipulation.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21387,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5349,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is a parameterized query used for?',NULL,'Parameterized queries keep supplied values separate from SQL syntax and are a key defense against SQL injection.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21391,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5350,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is a database role commonly used for?',NULL,'Database roles help manage permissions by grouping privileges into reusable security units.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21395,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5351,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What does the principle of least privilege mean for database access?',NULL,'Least privilege limits users and applications to only the permissions they need.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21399,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5352,95,112,'mcq_single','hard','What is a database transaction isolation problem caused by concurrent updates overwriting each other?',NULL,'A lost update occurs when one transaction\'s update overwrites another transaction\'s update without proper concurrency control.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21403,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5353,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is an entity in database modeling?',NULL,'An entity represents a distinguishable object or concept that the database stores information about.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21407,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5354,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is an attribute in a relational data model?',NULL,'An attribute is a property or characteristic of an entity and commonly corresponds to a table column.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21411,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5355,95,112,'mcq_single','easy','What is an ER diagram used to represent?',NULL,'An entity-relationship diagram models entities, their attributes, and relationships between them.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21415,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5356,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is a database migration?',NULL,'A migration is a versioned, controlled change to database schema or related data transformations.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21419,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5357,95,112,'mcq_single','hard','What is a materialized view?',NULL,'A materialized view stores query results physically and can be refreshed rather than recomputed for every access.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21423,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5358,95,112,'mcq_single','medium','What is an OLTP database primarily optimized for?',NULL,'OLTP systems are optimized for frequent, concurrent inserts, updates, deletes, and small reads.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21427,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 19:08:30','2026-08-15 19:08:30'),(5359,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','Where is the headquarters of RBSE located?',NULL,'The Board of Secondary Education, Rajasthan is headquartered in Ajmer.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21432,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5360,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','Which state education board is abbreviated as RBSE?',NULL,'RBSE is the abbreviation used for the Board of Secondary Education, Rajasthan.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21435,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5361,51,60,'mcq_single','medium','Which city is historically associated with the establishment of the Rajasthan Board of Secondary Education?',NULL,'The Rajasthan Board of Secondary Education was established with its headquarters at Ajmer.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21439,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5362,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','What is the main role of RBSE?',NULL,'RBSE is primarily responsible for school-level board examinations and related academic functions in Rajasthan.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21443,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5363,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','Which examination is conducted by RBSE for students completing secondary school?',NULL,'RBSE conducts the Secondary examination for students completing Class 10.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21447,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5364,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','Which RBSE examination is associated with completion of senior secondary school?',NULL,'The Senior Secondary examination is the Class 12 board examination conducted by RBSE.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21451,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5365,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','Which of these is an RBSE school-level examination category?',NULL,'Secondary is an RBSE school-level examination category, generally associated with Class 10.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21455,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5366,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','What does the term \'Senior Secondary\' generally refer to in RBSE?',NULL,'In RBSE, Senior Secondary refers to the higher secondary stage, including the Class 12 board examination.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21459,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5367,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','Which authority publishes RBSE board examination results?',NULL,'RBSE publishes results for examinations conducted by the Board of Secondary Education, Rajasthan.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21463,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5368,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','What is the official language commonly used for many RBSE question papers?',NULL,'Hindi is widely used in RBSE school examinations, alongside English and other permitted language options depending on the subject.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21467,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5369,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','Which class is commonly associated with the RBSE Secondary examination?',NULL,'The RBSE Secondary examination is the board examination for Class 10.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21471,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5370,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','Which class is commonly associated with the RBSE Senior Secondary examination?',NULL,'The RBSE Senior Secondary examination is the Class 12 board examination.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21475,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5371,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','Which board is responsible for the Rajasthan state school board curriculum and examinations?',NULL,'RBSE is Rajasthan\'s state board for school education and examinations.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21479,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5372,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','What does the \'S\' in RBSE represent?',NULL,'In RBSE, the letter S represents \'Secondary\' in the Board of Secondary Education, Rajasthan.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21483,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5373,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','What does the \'E\' in RBSE represent?',NULL,'The E in RBSE stands for Education.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21487,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5374,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','What does the \'B\' in RBSE represent?',NULL,'The B in RBSE stands for Board.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21491,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5375,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','What does the \'R\' in RBSE represent?',NULL,'The R in RBSE stands for Rajasthan.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21495,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5376,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','Which board is commonly called the Rajasthan Board?',NULL,'RBSE is commonly known as the Rajasthan Board.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21499,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5377,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','Which examination result is relevant to a student who completes Class 10 under RBSE?',NULL,'A Class 10 RBSE student receives a Secondary examination result.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21503,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5378,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','Which examination result is relevant to a student who completes Class 12 under RBSE?',NULL,'A Class 12 RBSE student receives a Senior Secondary examination result.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21507,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5379,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','Which organization provides the RBSE official examination timetable?',NULL,'The Board of Secondary Education, Rajasthan releases the official timetable for its board examinations.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21511,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5380,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','What is a board examination under RBSE?',NULL,'An RBSE board examination is a standardized school examination conducted under the authority of the Rajasthan Board.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21515,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5381,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','Which institution generally registers students for RBSE board examinations?',NULL,'Students normally appear through schools affiliated with the Rajasthan Board and registered for the relevant examination.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21519,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5382,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','What is the purpose of an RBSE admit card?',NULL,'The admit card contains candidate and examination details and authorizes the student to appear for the examination.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21523,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5383,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','Which document usually contains the student\'s marks after an RBSE board examination?',NULL,'The RBSE mark sheet records the marks or grades obtained in the relevant board examination.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21527,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5384,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','Which document may serve as proof of passing an RBSE board examination?',NULL,'A pass certificate can serve as official evidence that a student has passed the relevant board examination.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,21531,1,NULL,'2026-08-15 22:16:26','2026-08-15 22:16:26'),(5385,51,60,'mcq_single','easy','What