ity (MSF)?',NULL,'MSF is an overnight liquidity facility through which eligible banks can borrow from the RBI against eligible securities.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22111,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:43','2026-08-16 14:02:43'),(5530,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is liquidity in banking?',NULL,'Liquidity describes how readily an asset can be converted into cash without significant loss of value.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22115,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:43','2026-08-16 14:02:43'),(5531,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is a non-performing asset (NPA)?',NULL,'An NPA is a loan or advance classified as non-performing when it ceases to generate income for the bank according to prescribed norms.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22119,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:43','2026-08-16 14:02:43'),(5532,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is a secured loan?',NULL,'A secured loan is backed by collateral that provides security to the lender.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22123,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:43','2026-08-16 14:02:43'),(5533,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is an unsecured loan?',NULL,'An unsecured loan does not require specific collateral, although eligibility and credit assessment still apply.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22127,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:43','2026-08-16 14:02:43'),(5534,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What does EMI stand for?',NULL,'EMI stands for Equated Monthly Instalment and represents a regular repayment amount for many amortising loans.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22131,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:43','2026-08-16 14:02:43'),(5535,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','Which type of loan is specifically intended for purchasing a residential property?',NULL,'A home loan is generally used to finance the purchase, construction, or improvement of residential property.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22135,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:43','2026-08-16 14:02:43'),(5536,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','Which type of loan is primarily intended to finance education expenses?',NULL,'An education loan is designed to finance eligible educational expenses subject to lender and scheme conditions.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22139,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:43','2026-08-16 14:02:43'),(5537,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is a gold loan?',NULL,'A gold loan is generally secured by pledging eligible gold ornaments or other permitted gold assets.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22143,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:43','2026-08-16 14:02:43'),(5538,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is a cash credit facility?',NULL,'Cash credit is a working-capital facility that allows eligible borrowers to draw funds up to a sanctioned limit, usually against security.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22147,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:43','2026-08-16 14:02:43'),(5539,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is working capital?',NULL,'Working capital supports a business\'s routine operating needs, including short-term assets and liabilities.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22151,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:43','2026-08-16 14:02:43'),(5540,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is a letter of credit?',NULL,'A letter of credit is a bank undertaking to pay a beneficiary when specified documentary or contractual conditions are met.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22155,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:43','2026-08-16 14:02:43'),(5541,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is a bank guarantee?',NULL,'A bank guarantee is an undertaking by a bank to make payment to a beneficiary upon specified default or conditions.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22159,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:43','2026-08-16 14:02:43'),(5542,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is priority sector lending?',NULL,'Priority sector lending directs credit toward sectors identified by the RBI as important for broad-based and inclusive development.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22163,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:43','2026-08-16 14:02:43'),(5543,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','Which of the following is a priority sector category in India?',NULL,'Agriculture is one of the sectors covered under priority sector lending guidelines.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22167,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:43','2026-08-16 14:02:43'),(5544,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is financial inclusion?',NULL,'Financial inclusion aims to provide affordable and useful financial services to people and communities that are underserved.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22171,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5545,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is a Basic Savings Bank Deposit Account (BSBDA)?',NULL,'BSBDA is designed to provide basic banking services to customers, subject to applicable RBI conditions.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22175,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5546,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is a nominee in a bank account?',NULL,'A nominee is a person designated to receive the deposit proceeds after the account holder\'s death, subject to applicable legal provisions.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22179,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5547,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is a joint bank account?',NULL,'A joint account is maintained in the names of two or more account holders under agreed operating instructions.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22183,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5548,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is a passbook?',NULL,'A passbook records transactions and balances associated with a bank account.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22187,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5549,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is a cheque?',NULL,'A cheque is a written instrument directing a bank to pay a specified sum from the drawer\'s account, subject to applicable rules.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22191,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5550,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','Who is the drawer of a cheque?',NULL,'The drawer is the person who writes and issues the cheque.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22195,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5551,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','Who is the drawee of a cheque?',NULL,'The drawee is the bank directed to make payment under the cheque.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22199,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5552,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','Who is the payee of a cheque?',NULL,'The payee is the person or entity named to receive payment under the cheque.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22203,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5553,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is cheque crossing?',NULL,'Crossing generally directs that the cheque be collected through a bank rather than paid as ordinary cash over the counter.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22207,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5554,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What does an account payee crossing generally indicate?',NULL,'An account payee crossing indicates that the cheque should be collected for the account of the named payee, subject to applicable banking practice and law.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22211,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5555,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is cheque dishonour?',NULL,'Cheque dishonour occurs when the bank refuses payment of the cheque for a stated reason.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22215,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5556,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is stop payment of a cheque?',NULL,'Stop payment is an instruction requesting the bank not to honour a specified cheque, subject to applicable rules and timing.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22219,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5557,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is digital banking?',NULL,'Digital banking enables customers to access and use banking services through electronic channels such as mobile and internet banking.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22223,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5558,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is internet banking?',NULL,'Internet banking allows customers to perform eligible banking activities through an online banking platform.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22227,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5559,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is mobile banking?',NULL,'Mobile banking enables customers to access eligible banking services using mobile devices and applications.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22231,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5560,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is a UPI PIN used for?',NULL,'A UPI PIN is used to authenticate eligible UPI payment transactions.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22235,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5561,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','Which information should generally never be shared with another person for transaction authentication?',NULL,'An OTP is confidential authentication information and should not be shared with others.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22239,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5562,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is phishing in banking security?',NULL,'Phishing uses deceptive messages or websites to trick users into revealing sensitive information such as passwords or OTPs.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22243,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5563,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is a PIN in banking?',NULL,'PIN stands for Personal Identification Number and is used as an authentication credential in several banking services.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22247,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5564,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is a bank reconciliation statement?',NULL,'A bank reconciliation statement identifies and explains differences between the bank balance in accounting records and the bank statement.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22251,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5565,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is the primary function of a commercial bank?',NULL,'Commercial banks accept deposits and provide credit, payment, and other financial services.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22255,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5566,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is the main role of the RBI as monetary authority?',NULL,'The RBI conducts monetary policy with the objective of maintaining price stability while keeping the objective of growth in mind.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22259,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5567,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is currency issuance in India primarily associated with the RBI?',NULL,'The RBI issues most banknotes, while the Government of India issues the one-rupee note and coins.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22263,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5568,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','Who issues the one-rupee note in India?',NULL,'The one-rupee note is issued by the Government of India.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22267,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5569,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is the currency symbol of the Indian rupee?',NULL,'The official symbol of the Indian rupee is â‚¹.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22271,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5570,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is a bank\'s capital adequacy intended to measure?',NULL,'Capital adequacy measures whether a bank has sufficient capital relative to its risk-weighted exposures and related requirements.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22275,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5571,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is Basel III primarily concerned with?',NULL,'Basel III is an international regulatory framework focused on strengthening bank capital, liquidity, and risk management.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22279,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5572,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is credit risk?',NULL,'Credit risk is the possibility that a borrower or counterparty will fail to meet agreed financial obligations.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22283,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5573,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is market risk for a bank?',NULL,'Market risk arises from adverse movements in market variables such as interest rates, foreign exchange rates, and prices.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22287,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5574,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is operational risk?',NULL,'Operational risk includes losses arising from inadequate or failed internal processes, people, systems, or external events.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22291,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5575,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is liquidity risk for a bank?',NULL,'Liquidity risk is the possibility that a bank cannot meet its financial obligations when they fall due without unacceptable losses.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22295,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5576,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is asset-liability management (ALM)?',NULL,'ALM manages the composition and associated risks of assets and liabilities, including liquidity and interest-rate risk.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22299,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5577,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is a bank\'s net interest income?',NULL,'Net interest income is broadly the difference between interest income earned on assets and interest expense paid on liabilities.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22303,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5578,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is a bank\'s spread in lending generally related to?',NULL,'A bank\'s lending spread generally reflects the difference between lending rates and relevant funding or deposit costs, along with other pricing factors.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22307,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5579,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is CASA in banking?',NULL,'CASA stands for Current Account Savings Account and refers to current and savings deposits held with a bank.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22311,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5580,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','Why do banks maintain provisions against certain loans?',NULL,'Provisions help banks recognise and absorb expected or identified losses associated with credit exposures.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22315,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5581,246,248,'mcq_single','easy','What is a credit score used for?',NULL,'A credit score is a numerical indicator used by lenders to assess creditworthiness based on credit history and related factors.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22319,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5582,246,248,'mcq_single','medium','What is a loan-to-value ratio?',NULL,'Loan-to-value compares the amount of a loan with the value of the asset securing or supporting the loan.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22323,1,NULL,'2026-08-16 14:02:44','2026-08-16 14:02:44'),(5583,1,2,'mcq_single','medium','Which organisation has proposed interstate licence portability for healthcare professionals in India?',NULL,'NITI Aayog has proposed interstate licence portability so registered healthcare professionals can practise in another state without repeated registration processes or No Objection Certificates.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22327,1,NULL,'2026-08-17 06:20:16','2026-08-17 06:20:16'),(5584,1,2,'mcq_single','medium','The proposed interstate licence portability for healthcare professionals is intended primarily to avoid which requirement?',NULL,'The proposal aims to reduce repeated registration procedures and No Objection Certificate requirements when healthcare professionals move between states.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22331,1,NULL,'2026-08-17 06:20:16','2026-08-17 06:20:16'),(5585,1,2,'mcq_single','easy','On 17 August 2026, which state saw farmers gathering near the Khanauri-Data Singh Wala inter-state border point?',NULL,'Haryana Police sealed the Khanauri-Data Singh Wala border point as farmers gathered to enter Haryana.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22335,1,NULL,'2026-08-17 06:20:16','2026-08-17 06:20:16'),(5586,1,2,'mcq_single','easy','Students in Jharkhand planned to gherao whose residence on 20 August 2026?',NULL,'Jharkhand students announced plans to gherao Chief Minister Hemant Soren\'s residence over issues linked to JPSC and JSSC examinations.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,22339,1,NULL,'2026-08-17 06:20:16','2